---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Editorial automation"
  description="How Model Fieldnotes prepares automated briefings, reviews research, and releases open-source tools."
>
  <div class="shell page-content">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Methods & accountability</p>
      <h1>How the notes get made.</h1>
      <p>Useful summaries should make the evidence easier to inspect.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose standalone-prose">
      <h2>Signed writing and the Fieldbook</h2>
      <p>
        Notes attributed to Swapnil Upganlawar connect agent reliability,
        evaluation, and the economics of useful outcomes. Research and drafting
        may be AI-assisted; a byline is not evidence that an experiment was
        performed.
      </p>
      <p>
        The <a href="/fieldbook/">Agent Reliability Fieldbook</a> contains
        simulation-based guides. Outcomes come from deterministic rules, not
        live-model measurements. Each guide identifies the scenario revision,
        the repair, and what remains untested. Scheduled generation does not
        create or modify Fieldbook entries.
      </p>
      <p>
        Use <a href="/writing/rss.xml">the signed-writing feed</a> for personal
        notes, research collections, and guides, or{' '}
        <a href="/rss.xml">the combined feed</a> to include automated briefings.
      </p>
      <h2>Leadership & Organizations</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="/leadership/">Leadership & Organizations</a> pairs signed
        analysis with curated readings. Study findings, self-reported surveys,
        analyst forecasts, and personal recommendations are identified
        separately. Reading suggestions state when only a public preview or
        summary was accessible; they do not imply full-text review. This section
        is maintained separately from scheduled briefings.
      </p>
      <h2>Daily briefings</h2>
      <p>
        Entries labeled “Model Fieldnotes · Automated briefing” are AI-generated
        from accessible public sources. The workflow checks dates, supporting
        excerpts, duplicates, and source attribution, then runs a separate
        automated verification pass. These checks can miss mistakes; they are
        not human review. Original writing remains separately attributed to
        Swapnil Upganlawar.
      </p>
      <p>
        Daily publication is designed for a small selection of useful
        developments, not a complete news service. Quiet days, inaccessible
        sources, spending limits, or failed checks can mean no edition. Research
        papers and vendor results are reported findings unless we explicitly
        document a reproduction.
      </p>
      <h2>What needs review</h2>
      <p>
        Weekly five-paper selections go through review before publication.
        Regulatory interpretation, allegations, sensitive advice, personal
        opinions, and uncertain claims also require review. An automated
        briefing does not express a personal endorsement by Swapnil Upganlawar.
      </p>
      <h2>Open-source projects</h2>
      <p>
        Weekly candidates start with a bounded problem and a comparison with
        existing tools. Generated source is tested in an isolated environment
        without publishing credentials. Public repositories require approval of
        the exact candidate. Passing tests does not establish security or
        production readiness; project pages document limitations and beta
        status.
      </p>
      <h2>Sources, corrections, and history</h2>
      <p>
        Follow each entry’s original sources for context. We link to source
        material rather than republishing full articles. Publication history and
        corrections are visible in GitHub. Substantive corrections should update
        the article, its date, and a correction note.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="https://github.com/swapupg/swapupg.github.io/issues/new?title=Editorial%20correction">
          Report a correction ↗
        </a>
        . Please include the page, disputed statement, and supporting source.
      </p>
      <h2>Public workflow, limited scope</h2>
      <p>
        The workflows and spending controls are{' '}
        <a href="https://github.com/swapupg/swapupg.github.io/tree/main/automation">
          open source
        </a>
        . Publication can be paused, and schedules are best effort. There is no
        behavioral analytics, reader account, or email collection. See our{' '}
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy page</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
